{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545647-how-exactly-the-magic-purview-works","id":1545647,"title":"How exactly the Magic Purview Works?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-10T09:56:38-08:00","id":1545647,"title":"How exactly the Magic Purview Works?","content":"Self-explanatory title. I've been a bit confused about how it should work. What exactly it does? What can one do with Magic Marvels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28637-hasura","name":"Hasura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T21:25:27-08:00","id":1545675,"title":"","content":"It helps enhance the spells you can cast, primarily. The marvels question is interesting because theoretically the Magic Purview character could do anything with it, per their Innate Power, but it has to be something that relates to the primary themes of Sorcery AKA its Workings: Summoning, Binding, Shapechanging, Wonderment aka Illusions and Divining. So, I could summon a fire elemental with a Magic Marvel, but I couldn't bless an army with strength because that's not what Sorcery, and therefore the Magic Purview, does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T16:10:02-08:00","id":1547437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545647-how-exactly-the-magic-purview-works?p=1545675#post1545675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps enhance the spells you can cast, primarily. The marvels question is interesting because theoretically the Magic Purview character could do anything with it, per their Innate Power, but it has to be something that relates to the primary themes of Sorcery AKA its Workings: Summoning, Binding, Shapechanging, Wonderment aka Illusions and Divining. So, I could summon a fire elemental with a Magic Marvel, but I couldn't bless an army with strength because that's not what Sorcery, and therefore the Magic Purview, does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also confused.<br /> <br /> So you get the Purview and can/must buy Workings and Techniques? Or just using a Marvel suffices? I am totally confused here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because the rules of the purview state:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroes get <b>access </b>to a <b>single </b>Working,<br /> Demigods two and Gods three. They <b>may</b><br /> purchase Techniques as if they were Heroic<br /> Knacks, and may use any Knack slots for them. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-01-2025, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T22:43:16-08:00","id":1547444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545647-how-exactly-the-magic-purview-works?p=1547437#post1547437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am also confused.<br /> <br /> So you get the Purview and can/must buy Workings and Techniques? Or just using a Marvel suffices? I am totally confused here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because the rules of the purview state:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First, Workings are not &quot;bought&quot; the same way Boons are not &quot;bought,&quot; they are automatically acquired as you progress in a Tier. Techniques, as the text you quoted says, can be purchased as if they were Heroic Knacks.<br /> <br /> Now, before I say anything else, let's use the text for the Innate Power to establish our foundation:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Innate Power: You can tell at a glance if someone is a Sorcerer, as long as they aren\u2019t trying to mystically conceal that fact. Further, your mastery of magic gives you a sense for how to tap into the power of others, tracing the routes of their miracles with your own sorcery. When someone else performs a Marvel or Boon in your presence, for the rest of the scene, <u>you reduce the Legend cost to emulate that effect with the Magic Purview by 1 for the rest of the scene, to a minimum of 1.</u> </div> </div> </div>And then the text for Emulate Boons with a Marvel:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can use a marvel to replicate the effects of a Boon<br /> you don\u2019t know \u2014 even one that belongs to another Purview,<br /> <u>as long as you can describe how your Purview and motif let<br /> you emulate the effect.</u> </div> </div> </div>Now, the reason why I said that Magic Marvels have to relate to the Workings of Sorcery is because all Purviews are focused on only a few things. Fire can't teleport you somewhere unless you enter a pyre and out another to do so. Fire also can't make you super speedy unless you create a jet flame or something to that effect. And none of those examples are possible without a Motif that fits them. Magic Marvels relate primarily to the Workings of Sorcery because the Magic Purview is all about Sorcery first and foremost. It wouldn't make sense to allow the Magic Purview the ability to replicate ANY Marvel or Boon without an appropriate Motif and theming. Otherwise, what would the limitations of the Magic Purview be? Why would Odin need to be a God of War if being a God of Magic would allow him to do literally anything as a copycat?<br /> <br /> If the developers want to say otherwise, they are totally free to do so. What I'm saying is what I believe to be the intended usage of the Magic Purview: Able to be a jack-of-all-trades, but only when they have a method which can duplicate/replicate the other person's powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T20:57:54-08:00","id":1547569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545647-how-exactly-the-magic-purview-works?p=1547444#post1547444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Workings are not &quot;bought&quot; the same way Boons are not &quot;bought,&quot; they are automatically acquired as you progress in a Tier. Techniques, as the text you quoted says, can be purchased as if they were Heroic Knacks.<br /> <br /> Now, before I say anything else, let's use the text for the Innate Power to establish our foundation:<br /> <br /> <br /> And then the text for Emulate Boons with a Marvel:<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, the reason why I said that Magic Marvels have to relate to the Workings of Sorcery is because all Purviews are focused on only a few things. Fire can't teleport you somewhere unless you enter a pyre and out another to do so. Fire also can't make you super speedy unless you create a jet flame or something to that effect. And none of those examples are possible without a Motif that fits them. Magic Marvels relate primarily to the Workings of Sorcery because the Magic Purview is all about Sorcery first and foremost. It wouldn't make sense to allow the Magic Purview the ability to replicate ANY Marvel or Boon without an appropriate Motif and theming. Otherwise, what would the limitations of the Magic Purview be? Why would Odin need to be a God of War if being a God of Magic would allow him to do literally anything as a copycat?<br /> <br /> If the developers want to say otherwise, they are totally free to do so. What I'm saying is what I believe to be the intended usage of the Magic Purview: Able to be a jack-of-all-trades, but only when they have a method which can duplicate/replicate the other person's powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Totally clear now that I have read both the Scion Hero Marvels section and your comment.<br /> <br /> <br /> A few other questions, since Sorcerers can buy Relics:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do they get access to a Purview Innate Power?</li> <li>IF the first answer is yes, would Sorcerers get the ability to use Marvels (I think no) for said Purview?</li> <li>IF the first answer is yes, with the Magic Purview, do they get access to another Working? (I think no)</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-08-2025, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T17:19:28-08:00","id":1547637,"title":"","content":"We need a Sorcerers book that reflects the <b>Scion</b> game. It should include mythologically correct magics of at least three or four cultures. And, because apotheosis was a goal of many real word Occult practitioners, and some Egyptian myths even say that Isis was a <i>mortal </i>woman who achieved godhood through sorcery, we need mechanics for apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T17:33:36-08:00","id":1547639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545647-how-exactly-the-magic-purview-works?p=1547637#post1547637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a Sorcerers book that reflects the <b>Scion</b> game. It should include mythologically correct magics of at least three or four cultures. And, because apotheosis was a goal of many real word Occult practitioners, and some Egyptian myths even say that Isis was a <i>mortal </i>woman who achieved godhood through sorcery, we need mechanics for apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Total agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T10:41:42-08:00","id":1547647,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers have Legend. It's stolen Legend; but it's still Legend. I would allow a Sorcerer who works his way up on Legend to eventually unlock a Demigod-like status, which could then be leveraged all the way up to apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T15:29:54-08:00","id":1547652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545647-how-exactly-the-magic-purview-works?p=1547647#post1547647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers have Legend. It's stolen Legend; but it's still Legend. I would allow a Sorcerer who works his way up on Legend to eventually unlock a Demigod-like status, which could then be leveraged all the way up to apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apollonius of Tyana would be a Demigod example. Some forms of Isis would be the god level example. Medea, Merlin, Morgan le Fay, would be nearly gods. There are some Native American medicine people who seem to have becomed worshipped after death. So achieving apotheosis by hard work and talent isn't something mythology doesn't embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}